<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32839" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">optātĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				wishing</i>, <i>a wish</i> (class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Theseo cum tres optationes Neptunus dedisset,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Off. 3, 25, 94</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Rhet. fig., <i>the expression of a wish</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">optatio atque exsecratio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 3, 53, 205</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Quint. 9, 1, 32, 9, 2,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A choosing</i>, <i>choice</i>, <i><span class="en">Symm. Ep.
				1, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
